		<dict>
			<key>FooterText</key>
			<string>Used only when Palette is Custom. Six hex digits, as on the web: 2D2D2D, #2D2D2D and 0x2D2D2D are all accepted. A field left empty, or holding anything else, falls back to the Default color for that slot — so one typo costs you one color, not the page.

Nothing here is checked for legibility. Ink and paper set to similar colors will produce a page you cannot read; that is the point of typing it yourself rather than picking from the list.

The button pad follows the paper color, so its outlines stay a fixed step away from whatever you choose. The contrast figures printed on the Button Pad rows are measured against the Default paper and will be approximate against a custom one.</string>
